    "body": "Thank you for your great work. I am currently reading the paper and trying to reproduce and understand the quantization experiments on ```OpenVLA```.\n\nI noticed that the paper compares ```QVLA``` with several quantization baselines, including ```AWQ``` and ```SmoothQuant```. I would like to ask a few questions about the implementation details of these baselines:\n\n1. Which quantization framework or codebase was used for the ```AWQ``` and ```SmoothQuant``` baselines on ```OpenVLA```?\n· For example, were they based on ```AutoAWQ```, ```llm-awq```, the official ```SmoothQuant``` implementation, Hugging Face Transformers, ```vLLM```, or a custom implementation?\n2. What inference backend was used to evaluate the quantized models?\n· For example, Hugging Face Transformers, ```vLLM```,``` SGLang```, ```TensorRT-LLM```, ```PyTorch eager mode```, or custom CUDA kernels?\n3. Could you share the specific quantization configuration used for the ```AWQ / SmoothQuant``` baselines?\n· For example, the weight and activation bit-widths.\n\n\nThese details would be very helpful for reproducing the experiments and for better understanding the practical acceleration effects of quantization on VLA models.\n\nThank you very much!",
